<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Salé</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Salé is a city on the Atlantic coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a>, on the north bank of the Bou Regreg estuary opposite <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rabat">Rabat</a>. Founded in the 11th century, it became a trading and religious centre, and in the 17th century it was a base of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barbary-coast">Barbary</a> corsairs known as the Salé Rovers, whose Republic of Salé raided shipping as far as Iceland. It is now part of the Rabat–Salé conurbation.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sale.jpg" alt="Salé" width="320" height="402" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ismael zniber and Bertramz for Sale,BabMrisa.jpg · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Monuments_de_Sal%C3%A9.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
